# The one list of test files. ./verify.sh runs it through `node tests/run.mjs --local`,
# each CI job through `node tests/run.mjs <group>`; tests/suite-coverage.mjs fails when a
# test file (tests/*.mjs, packs/*/tests/*.mjs) is not here once, or a lane has no gate.
#
# One file per line, in run order:  <path>  <lane>...  [# reason]
#   ci:<group>   runs in the CI job that runs <group>, and in verify.sh; a file may name
#                more than one group
#   ci-only      with ci:<group>: CI only, never verify.sh
#   local        verify.sh only
#   pending-ci   in no gate yet: PR 2 (tests/) and PR 3 (packs/) of
#                builds/ci-one-list/plan.md give these files CI jobs and remove the lane
#   manual       run by hand, never by a gate
#   helper       not a test: a module or script other files run
# local, pending-ci, manual and helper need a reason after #. Lines starting with # are
# comments.
#
# package and bunx keep their own steps in ci.yml (they take the packed tarball);
# suite-coverage checks that those steps name the files tagged for them.

